cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use groupeval, please cite it."
title: "groupeval: evaluation that respects the group structure benchmarks actually have"
abstract: >-
  Tools for benchmarks built from groups (video frames of one lesion, slices of one scan, crops of
  one slide, images of one patient) where scores are conventionally reported as if every file were
  an independent observation. Provides exact duplicate audits, group-disjoint split construction
  with leakage assertions, cluster-bootstrap and paired intervals, and a variance decomposition that
  separates "needs more compute" from "needs more data".
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hossain
    given-names: Samir
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8986-0946"
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Texas Tech University"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - benchmark evaluation
  - data leakage
  - clustered data
  - confidence intervals
  - reproducibility
